##
#
# Well-balancing test for a 1D isothermal steady state [1] in the
# configuration of [2], Section 4.1.4 (Table 4.4) of [3].
#
# The initial state is the isothermal equilibrium
#
#   rho_e = exp(-(x - 2)),  p_e = exp(-(x - 2)),  v = 0,
#   theta = (1 / rho_e) * p_e^(1/gamma),
#
# on the computational domain [0,5] with slip boundary conditions. The
# thermodynamic constants are p_0 = 1, c_v = 2.5, gamma = 1.4 (thus R = 1)
# and g = 1. The final time is t = 0.8 with CFL 0.05.
#
# The scheme preserves the isothermal equilibrium exactly, i.e., up to
# round-off errors. Table 4.4 of [3] uses 100, 200, ..., 3200 subdivisions.
# The tabulated error is the sum of the normalized errors of rho and
# rho_theta (this file) and the unnormalized error of m (which vanishes
# identically and cannot be normalized); the latter is obtained by setting
# "error quantities = m" and "error normalize = false".
#
# [1] R. J. LeVeque, D. S. Bale. Wave propagation methods for conservation
#     laws with source terms. In: M. Fey, R. Jeltsch (eds.), Hyperbolic
#     Problems: Theory, Numerics, Applications, pp. 609-618, Birkhäuser,
#     1999. DOI 10.1007/978-3-0348-8724-3_12
#
# [2] A. Navas-Montilla, I. Echeverribar. A family of well-balanced WENO and
#     TENO schemes for atmospheric flows. J. Comput. Phys., 489:112273,
#     2023. DOI 10.1016/j.jcp.2023.112273
#
# [3] C. Farris, M. Maier, E. J. Tovar. Well-balanced second-order
#     approximation of the compressible atmospheric Euler equations.
#     Preprint, 2026. arXiv:2606.19764
#
##

subsection A - Scheduler
  set basename          = isothermal-well-balanced
  set tasks             = error evaluation
  set final time        = 0.8
  set timer granularity = 0.008
end

subsection B - Equation
  set dimension          = 1
  set equation           = euler atmospheric
  set c_v                = 2.5
  set gamma              = 1.4
  set gravity            = 1
  set reference pressure = 1
end

subsection C - Discretization
  set geometry        = rectangular domain
  set mesh refinement = 0

  subsection rectangular domain
    set position bottom left     = 0
    set position top right       = 5
    set subdivisions x           = 200
    set boundary condition left  = slip
    set boundary condition right = slip
  end
end

subsection E - InitialValues
  set configuration = function
  set position      = 0

  subsection function
    set density expression               = exp(-x+2)
    set velocity x expression            = 0
    set potential temperature expression = (1/exp(-x+2)) * (exp(-x+2))^(1/1.4)
  end
end

subsection H - TimeIntegrator
  set cfl min = 0.05
  set cfl max = 0.05
end

subsection K - ErrorEvaluation
  set error quantities = rho, rho_theta
  set error normalize  = true
  set error norms      = Linf, L1, L2
end
